DentQ Admin — Analytics Dashboard: Full Implementation Prompt

Architecture overview
The dashboard is the default landing page of the admin panel, rendered at the /admin or /admin/dashboard route. It is a single scrollable page — no sub-navigation — divided into six visual rows. All data is fetched from Supabase using parallel queries on mount. A time-range selector (7d / 30d / 90d / All time) at the top-right re-fetches all queries when changed. The page renders with skeleton placeholders while data loads, then swaps them for real content. All monetary values are in EGP. All numbers are formatted with Intl.NumberFormat('en-EG') for thousands separators.

Data fetching strategy
All queries run in parallel via Promise.all on component mount and on every time-range change. The time-range filter is applied by passing a from date to every query as a .gte('created_at', fromDate) clause. The fromDate is computed from the selected range button: 7 days, 30 days, 90 days ago, or null for all time.
The useDashboard hook returns a single data object with all computed values, a loading boolean, and a range state with a setRange setter. The hook memoizes the computed metrics so they don't recalculate on re-renders unrelated to data changes.

Row 1 — Time-range selector and page header
The topbar is a flex row with the page title and date on the left, and four pill-style buttons on the right (7d, 30d, 90d, All time). The active pill has background: var(--color-text-primary) and color: var(--color-background-primary). Only one pill is active at a time. Clicking a pill updates the range state in the hook, which triggers a re-fetch.

Row 2 — Primary KPI cards (4 cards)
Each card uses the metric card pattern: background: var(--color-background-secondary), no border, border-radius: var(--border-radius-md). Inside each card: a small icon + muted label at the top, the metric value in 22px/500 weight, a delta badge showing percent change vs the previous equivalent period, and a 28px-tall sparkline chart at the bottom.
Card 1 — Total revenue
Query: SELECT SUM(total_amount) FROM "Orders" WHERE created_at >= fromDate AND status != 'cancelled'.
Delta: compare current period sum to previous period sum (same duration, shifted back). Show green arrow up or red arrow down with percentage.
Sparkline: daily revenue bucketed by date. Line chart, no axes, no labels, blue (#378ADD).
Card 2 — Total orders
Query: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "Orders" WHERE created_at >= fromDate.
Delta: count current vs previous period. Sparkline: daily order count, green (#639922).
Card 3 — New clients
Query: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "Clients" WHERE created_at >= fromDate.
Delta: vs previous period. Sparkline: daily new client registrations, purple (#7F77DD).
Card 4 — Average order value (AOV)
Computed: total_revenue / total_orders (exclude cancelled orders from both numerator and denominator).
Delta: vs previous period AOV. Sparkline: daily AOV, amber (#EF9F27).

Row 3 — Secondary KPI cards (4 cards, same visual style)
Card 1 — Gross profit
Query: SELECT SUM(p.profit * oi.quantity) FROM "Order_items" oi JOIN "Products" p ON p.id = oi.product_id JOIN "Orders" o ON o.id = oi.order_id WHERE o.created_at >= fromDate AND o.status != 'cancelled'.
Show computed margin percentage: (profit / revenue * 100).toFixed(1)% as the sub-label.
Card 2 — Promo discounts given
Query: SELECT SUM(discount) FROM "Orders" WHERE created_at >= fromDate AND discount > 0.
Sub-label: (discount_total / revenue * 100).toFixed(1)% of revenue.
Card 3 — Pending orders
Query: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "Orders" WHERE status = 'pending'. Note: no date filter — this is always the live current count. The value renders in amber (#854F0B) to signal it needs attention.
Card 4 — Cancelled orders
Query: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "Orders" WHERE created_at >= fromDate AND status = 'cancelled'.
Sub-label: (cancelled / total * 100).toFixed(1)% cancel rate. Value renders in red (#A32D2D).

Row 4 — Revenue over time chart + Order status donut
Left (2/3 width) — Revenue over time line chart
Chart.js line type. Two datasets: Revenue (solid blue #378ADD, borderWidth: 2) and Profit (dashed green #97C459, borderDash: [4,4], borderWidth: 2). Both have pointRadius: 0 and tension: 0.4 for smooth curves. No fill. X-axis: dates bucketed by day (7d/30d) or by week (90d) or by month (all time) — the bucket size adapts to the range. Y-axis ticks formatted as Nk (divide by 1000, append k). X-axis tick count capped at 8 using maxTicksLimit: 8. Grid lines use var(--color-border-tertiary).
Query for revenue series: SELECT DATE(created_at) as day, SUM(total_amount) as rev FROM "Orders" WHERE created_at >= fromDate AND status != 'cancelled' GROUP BY day ORDER BY day.
Query for profit series: same join as gross profit query above, grouped by day.
Custom HTML legend above the chart (not Chart.js built-in): two items — blue square for Revenue, green dashed-border square for Profit.
Right (1/3 width) — Order status donut + horizontal bar breakdown
Chart.js doughnut type with cutout: '68%'. Five segments: Delivered (green #639922), Shipped (blue #378ADD), Paid (purple #7F77DD), Pending (amber #EF9F27), Cancelled (red #E24B4A). borderWidth: 0. No built-in legend.
Below the donut: a manually built horizontal bar list. Each row has: status label (fixed 68px width), a thin progress bar (height 7px, fill color matching the donut segment, background var(--color-background-secondary)), and a right-aligned count. The bar width percentage is (statusCount / totalOrders * 100)%.
Query: SELECT status, COUNT(*) FROM "Orders" WHERE created_at >= fromDate GROUP BY status.

Row 5 — Three equal-width cards
Card 1 — Top products by revenue
Query: SELECT p."nameEn", SUM(oi.quantity * oi.price) as total FROM "Order_items" oi JOIN "Products" p ON p.id = oi.product_id JOIN "Orders" o ON o.id = oi.order_id WHERE o.created_at >= fromDate AND o.status != 'cancelled' GROUP BY p.id, p."nameEn" ORDER BY total DESC LIMIT 5.
Render as a vertical list. Each row: rank number (muted, fixed 14px width), product name (truncated with ellipsis), revenue value right-aligned in font-weight: 500.
Card 2 — Top products by units sold
Same join but order by SUM(oi.quantity) DESC. Show units count instead of revenue.
Card 3 — Revenue by category (donut)
Query: SELECT c.name_en, SUM(oi.quantity * oi.price) as total FROM "Order_items" oi JOIN "Products" p ON p.id = oi.product_id JOIN "Categories" c ON c.id = p.category_id JOIN "Orders" o ON o.id = oi.order_id WHERE o.created_at >= fromDate AND o.status != 'cancelled' GROUP BY c.id, c.name_en ORDER BY total DESC LIMIT 4.
Chart.js doughnut with cutout: '60%'. Four segments with the blue/green/purple/amber palette. Custom HTML legend above showing category name + percentage of total.

Row 6 — Two equal-width cards
Card 1 — Orders by governorate (horizontal bars)
Query: SELECT gs."governorateEn", COUNT(*) as cnt FROM "Orders" o JOIN "GovernoratesShipping" gs ON gs.id = o.governorate_id WHERE o.created_at >= fromDate GROUP BY gs."governorateEn" ORDER BY cnt DESC LIMIT 7.
Render as a stacked list of rows: governorate name (fixed 80px, truncated), horizontal progress bar (height 6px, blue #85B7EB, width relative to the top governorate's count = 100%), order count right-aligned in muted text.
Card 2 — Promo code performance
Top section: three inline stat cards in a 3-column grid — Active codes (live count from promo_codes where is_active = true), Total uses (sum of array_length(used_by_user_ids, 1) for the period... or count of orders with a non-null promocode_id in the period), Total EGP discounted (sum of discount from orders with a promo in the period).
Below: a ranked list of promo codes by usage. Each row: code in monospace (fixed 80px), horizontal bar (blue #85B7EB, width relative to top code = 100%), uses count right-aligned.
Query: SELECT pc.code, COUNT(o.id) as uses, SUM(o.discount) as total_discount FROM promo_codes pc JOIN "Orders" o ON o.promocode_id = pc.id WHERE o.created_at >= fromDate GROUP BY pc.id, pc.code ORDER BY uses DESC LIMIT 5.

Row 7 — Two equal-width cards
Card 1 — Orders by payment method (horizontal bar chart)
Query: SELECT payment_method, COUNT(*) as cnt FROM "Orders" WHERE created_at >= fromDate GROUP BY payment_method.
Chart.js bar with indexAxis: 'y' (horizontal). Three bars: Cash on delivery (blue #B5D4F4), Credit card (purple #AFA9EC), PayPal (teal #5DCAA5). borderRadius: 4. X-axis ticks formatted as N orders. Custom legend above chart.
Card 2 — Recent activity feed
Not a chart — a live event log. Fetch the 6 most recent events by combining:

Last 6 orders: SELECT id, status, total_amount, created_at FROM "Orders" ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 6
Last 3 client registrations: SELECT "fullName", created_at FROM "Clients" ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 3
Products with stock < 5: SELECT "nameEn", stock FROM "Products" WHERE stock < 5 ORDER BY stock ASC LIMIT 3

Merge, sort by created_at descending, take top 6. Each row: a 7px colored dot (green for delivered, blue for new client, amber for low stock, red for cancelled, purple for promo use), a text description with a bold entity name, and a relative time label ("2m ago", "1h ago") computed from created_at using a timeAgo(date) helper.

Row 8 — Full-width grouped bar chart
Monthly revenue vs profit — full year
Only shown when range is "All time" or "90d". Otherwise hidden.
Chart.js bar type. Two datasets side-by-side per month: Revenue bars (light blue fill #B5D4F4, blue border #378ADD) and Profit bars (light green fill #C0DD97, green dashed border #639922, borderDash: [3,3]). borderRadius: 4. borderSkipped: false. 12 months on X-axis. Y-axis ticks formatted as Nk.
Query: SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', created_at) as month, SUM(total_amount) as rev FROM "Orders" WHERE status != 'cancelled' GROUP BY month ORDER BY month — same for profit via the order_items join.

Supporting component: DeltaBadge
Props: value (number, the % change), inverted (bool — for metrics where a decrease is good, like cancellations).
Renders: a small flex row with an up or down chevron SVG (10×10) and the formatted percentage. Green color (#3B6D11) for positive (or negative if inverted), red (#A32D2D) for the other direction. Text: +18.4% or -3.1%. Uses Math.abs(value).toFixed(1).

Supporting component: Sparkline
Props: data (array of numbers), color (hex string).
Renders a Chart.js line chart inside a 28px-tall div. pointRadius: 0, borderWidth: 1.5, fill: false, no axes, no grid, no tooltip, tension: 0.4. The component takes data directly — the parent passes pre-bucketed daily values.

Skeleton loading state
While loading is true, every card renders a skeleton version: a var(--color-background-secondary) rectangle with border-radius: var(--border-radius-md) and the same dimensions as the real content. Skeleton cards animate with a simple CSS opacity pulse (@keyframes pulse { 0%,100%{opacity:1} 50%{opacity:.5} }). Charts show a flat gray rectangle at the same height. The topbar and time-range buttons are not skeletonized — they render immediately.

What NOT to build on this page

